-    Match case/symbol names exactly; similar names are not matches. Summarize each item with observed file/range or "not found in observed source". Do not infer defaults, copy excerpts/IDs, or discuss adjacent cases.
-    Submit via submit_artifact with top-level source_refs:["all"]; leave blocks/evidence_refs empty. Use [] only without captures. Buckley supplies captured bytes, not summary verification.
-    Use incomplete with specific incomplete_reasons for missing items, unread pages, unavailable references, or exhausted budgets; retain usable captures.
+    Stay within requested files/ranges. In caller-named files, read_file BEFORE searches: honor ranges; otherwise read the first page for whole-file scope, or a unique literal anchor for targeted excerpts. After an anchor miss, read a page there before searching again. Follow next_start_line for unread pages while budget permits. Search unknown files with search_text literal:true for exact text.
+    Match symbols exactly; similar names are not matches. Give one short sentence per requested symbol: name, observed behavior, filename or "not found in observed source". No line numbers/ranges, excerpts/IDs, padding commentary, adjacent declarations, or inferred defaults in summary prose. Host-captured evidence owns exact path/range/bytes, not summary verification.
+    Submit via submit_artifact with top-level source_refs:["all"]; leave blocks/evidence_refs empty. Use [] only without captures.
+    Use incomplete with specific incomplete_reasons for missing items, unread ranges, unavailable references, or exhausted budgets; retain usable captures.
     If tools are disabled, use JSON fallback with the same selector. No edits, commands, tests, credentials, or recommendations.
 tools:
   tier: read_only
